  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (sentiment ≤ 0.00) to counteract overconfidence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — apply a lag correction (e.g., 3-5 day smoothing) to avoid overshoots.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is > 10% above recent 10-day average, reduce by 5-10% to align with historical volatility.",
    "For high sentiment (sentiment > 0.50), reduce forecast by 3-5% to account for overreaction or speculative bias.",
    "When true outcome is consistently higher than forecast (e.g., > 5% over 30d), apply a ‘recovery bias’ — increase forecast by 2-5% for next period to reflect momentum.",
    "If forecast is consistently below true outcome (e.g., < 5% under 30d), apply a ‘lag correction’ — add 1-3% to forecast to account for delayed market response."
  ]
}
